<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/13th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Lipitsa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1216">1216</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Lipitsa was fought in April 1216 near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuryev-polsky">Yuryev-Polsky</a> between the sons of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vsevolod-the-big-nest">Vsevolod the Big Nest</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/konstantin-of-rostov">Konstantin of Rostov</a>, allied with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mstislav-mstislavich">Mstislav the Bold</a> of Novgorod, defeated his brothers Yuri and Yaroslav, whose army suffered heavy losses. The victory made Konstantin grand prince of Vladimir, and the battle is remembered as one of the bloodiest fought between Rus' princes.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Internal wars proved as costly as foreign ones: at the <b>Battle of Lipitsa</b> in 1216 Mstislav the Bold of Novgorod and Konstantin of Rostov routed the brothers Yuri and Yaroslav, with heavy losses on the Suzdalian side.</blockquote><a href="/empire/vladimir-suzdal">Vladimir-Suzdal · Military</a></li></ul></section>
